{"created": "2026-09-12T08:39:54.789266+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-13T04:20:51.056380+00:00", "id": 22722557, "conceptrecid": "22722556", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22722557", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22722556", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722557", "metadata": {"title": "Mori\u2013Zwanzig Perspective on Neural Representation Dynamics: Coarse-Graining via Short-Memory Closure", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22722557", "publication_date": "2026-09-12", "description": "<p>We study layerwise neural representation dynamics through a coarse-grained reduced-dynamics lens. From a Mori&ndash;Zwanzig perspective, selected representation summaries are treated as resolved variables, while the remaining degrees of freedom are treated as unresolved variables whose elimination induces memory effects. This leads to an operational criterion for coarse-state quality: a useful coarse state should support an accurate short-memory closure of the depth-wise dynamics.</p>\n<p>We derive a local resolved&ndash;unresolved surrogate showing that short-memory closure is promoted by contraction in the unresolved directions, weak cross-subspace coupling, and stable transport along task-relevant resolved directions. This connects coarse-state closure to task-relevant geometry preservation without requiring global dynamical isometry. Empirically, we fit reduced models to candidate coarse states extracted from trained neural networks across synthetic tasks and architectures. The results show that closure quality is related to, but not determined by, predictive accuracy, and that the most suitable coarse state depends strongly on task structure and architectural bias. These findings suggest that coarse-state selection is fundamentally a reduced-modeling problem rather than a purely heuristic choice of representation summary.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Watanabe, Kosuke", "affiliation": "Reitaku University", "orcid": "0009-0004-1917-4390"}], "keywords": ["Mori\u2013Zwanzig formalism", "neural representation dynamics", "neural network dynamics", "coarse-graining", "short-memory closure", "reduced-order modeling", "deep neural networks", "representation learning"], "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22722556"}}]}}, "title": "Mori\u2013Zwanzig Perspective on Neural Representation Dynamics: Coarse-Graining via Short-Memory Closure", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722557", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22722557", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22722557?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722557", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722557", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22722557", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722557/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722556", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22722556", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722556", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22722556", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22722557/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22722557/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722557/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722557/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22722557:Mori_Zwanzig_Neural_Representation_Dynamics_preprint.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22722557:Mori_Zwanzig_Neural_Representation_Dynamics_preprint.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22722557:Mori_Zwanzig_Neural_Representation_Dynamics_preprint.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22722557:Mori_Zwanzig_Neu